<title>USA: Southern 812 MW Ala. nuke shut for refueling.</title>
<headline>Southern 812 MW Ala. nuke shut for refueling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Co's 812 megawatt Farley nuclear power unit 1 was shut Saturday as expected for about 50 days of scheduled maintenance and refueling, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Dothan, Ala., is expected to return to service in early May, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The adjacent 822 megawatt Farley unit 2 continued to operate normally at 100 percent of capacity as of early Monday, the NRC said.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
